{"id":"neet-2026-q012","pn":12,"y":"NEET 2026 · 21 Jun · Re-exam","tp":"Alternating Current","st":"Series LCR resonance","q":"An ac voltage V = 220 sin(2 × 10³t) Volt is applied to a series LCR circuit. Then the current amplitude in this circuit is:\n(Given : L = 10 mH, C = 25 μF, R = 100 Ω)","o":["5.5 A","11.0 A","22.0 A","2.2 A"],"c":3,"s":"Angular frequency of the source ω = 2 × 10³ rad/s.\nInductive reactance X_L = ωL = (2 × 10³) × (10 × 10⁻³) = 20 Ω.\nCapacitive reactance X_C = 1/(ωC) = 1/[(2 × 10³) × (25 × 10⁻⁶)] = 20 Ω.\nX_L = X_C, so the circuit is at resonance and impedance Z = R.\nCurrent amplitude i₀ = V₀/Z = V₀/R = 220/100 = 2.2 A."},
{"id":"neet-2025-q016","pn":16,"y":"NEET 2025","tp":"Alternating Current","st":"Series LCR circuit","q":"To an ac power supply of 220 V at 50 Hz, a resistor of 20 Ω, a capacitor of reactance 25 Ω and an inductor of reactance 45 Ω are connected in series. The corresponding current in the circuit and the phase angle between the current and the voltage is, respectively","o":["7.8 A and 30°","7.8 A and 45°","15.6 A and 30°","15.6 A and 45°"],"c":1,"s":"X_L = 45 Ω, X_C = 25 Ω, R = 20 Ω\nI = 220/√((X_L − X_C)² + R²) = 220/√((45 − 25)² + 20²)\nI = 220/(2√2) = 11/√2 = 7.779 A\ntan φ = (X_L − X_C)/R = (45 − 25)/20 = 1\nφ = 45°"}
